            <div xml:id="d795">

                <pb facs="0963" n="873" sameAs="frus:frus1920v02/pg873"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">815.51/391: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul in Chargé of the Legation in Honduras</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Lawton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-04-17T15:00:00-05:48"><hi rendition="#italic">April 17,
                                1920—3 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 11:25
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>38. Department’s March 23, 6 p.m. The Honduranean Government offers Professor
                    Kemmerer one thousand American dollars a month not exceeding six [months] and
                    five hundred dollars travel expenses. Full report by mail.<anchor n="18"
                        xml:id="d795-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lawton</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
